  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 6026,
  "title": "Bump body-parser to 2.4.0 in the lockfile",
  "body": "> Clears Dependabot alerts [#2554](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/security/dependabot/2554) (GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828, high) and [#2387](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/security/dependabot/2387) (GHSA-v422-hmwv-36x6, low): the lockfile resolves `body-parser@2.2.1`.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- 👷🏻 Test servers: bumped [`body-parser@2.4.0`](https://npmjs.com/package/body-parser/v/2.4.0), clearing 2 security alerts, in PR [#6026](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6026), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\n`body-parser` comes only from `express@5.2.1` in the private `test-harness` and `test-web-server` packages, which mount no body parser. `npm update body-parser` moves it to 2.4.0, which `express`'s `^2.2.1` already allows, so no `package.json` changes.\n\n## Design\n\n- Lockfile only, instead of bumping `express` to 5.3.0 in 2 `package.json` files or adding `overrides`.\n- `minimatch` (GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249) is not part of this PR: it is only patched in 11.x, a rewrite that `glob@10` (used by `test-exclude` and `cldr-data`) cannot use, as it no longer returns RegExp parts.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `package-lock.json`: `body-parser` 2.2.1 → 2.4.0, its `iconv-lite` 0.7.2 → 0.7.3, `type-is` 2.0.1 → 2.1.0, and `content-type@2.1.0` nested under both\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
